<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warangal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Orugallu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Warangal, historically Orugallu, is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and was the capital of the Kakatiya dynasty from the late 12th century. Its fort, with great stone gateways, was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> in 1323, recovered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musunuri-nayakas">Musunuri Nayaks</a> in the 1330s and later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>. It is now one of the largest cities in Telangana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warangal.jpg" alt="Warangal" width="286" height="549" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JohnnyBlaze007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WarangalMontage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
